  "fill": {
   "season": "Jun-Sep",
   "overview": "A straight line up the west side of Mount Jefferson to the summit pinnacle. The lower ridge is moderate snow; the pinnacle is sound rock. Protection is rarely needed until the pinnacle, so most parties carry a few pickets or screws for the snow and a light rack of nuts and slings for the top. The face holds shade well into the morning.",
   "approach": "Reached from the west off the Pacific Crest Trail, starting from either the Pamelia Lake or the Woodpecker Ridge trailhead. The walk in is long; check which permit applies to the trailhead you choose.",
   "descent_text": "Reverse the ridge, or traverse north around the pinnacle to its east side and downclimb loose fourth-class rock from there. Rockfall is common."
